{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":8362,"name":"","username":"bubb1es","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/delvingbitcoin.org/bubb1es/{size}/1785_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-22T05:13:29.999Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIn light of recent events I became interested in how to safely generate a strong random seed. The closest tool I found in rust is \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/BlockchainCommons/seedtool-cli-rust\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eseedtool-cli-rust\u003c/a\u003e but it has a lot of dependencies I don’t recognize and I prefer building on the rust-bitcoin orgs crates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI humbly submit my own cli tool \u003ccode\u003eseedroller\u003c/code\u003e for generating BIP39 seed words from dice rolls hashed with \u003ccode\u003egetrandom()\u003c/code\u003e system entropy. I also created a companion cli tool \u003ccode\u003ekeyderiver\u003c/code\u003e that takes your seed words and derives BIP380 descriptor key expressions. Both are based on rust-bitcoin org rust crates and have minimal other dependencies. For all the fun details please checkout the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/bubb1es71/bitcoin-key-tools\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ebitcoin-key-tools\u003c/a\u003e repo.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFeedback is much appreciated, this is still early work and I’m happy to implement suggestions that improve these tools soundness and security.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-22T05:13:29.999Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":43,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":217.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":2822,"topic_slug":"seedroller-and-keyderiver-cli-tools-to-generate-bip39-seed-words-and-derive-bip380-keys","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://github.com/BlockchainCommons/seedtool-cli-rust","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - BlockchainCommons/seedtool-cli-rust: A command-line tool for generating and transforming cryptographic seeds. · GitHub","clicks":2},{"url":"https://github.com/bubb1es71/bitcoin-key-tools","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - bubb1es71/bitcoin-key-tools: Security-sensitive command-line tools for Bitcoin key management. · GitHub","clicks":2}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1049,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/seedroller-and-keyderiver-cli-tools-to-generate-bip39-seed-words-and-derive-bip380-keys/2822/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":8374,"name":"Anzus","username":"Anzus_GemWallet","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/delvingbitcoin.org/anzus_gemwallet/{size}/2271_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-24T10:42:47.920Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis looks interesting. For people using dice because they want to avoid relying on a computer for randomness, would it make sense to offer a clearly labelled dice-only option as well?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat could make it easier for users to understand exactly what they are trusting and choose the approach they are comfortable with.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-24T10:42:47.920Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":1.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":2822,"topic_slug":"seedroller-and-keyderiver-cli-tools-to-generate-bip39-seed-words-and-derive-bip380-keys","display_username":"Anzus","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1377,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/seedroller-and-keyderiver-cli-tools-to-generate-bip39-seed-words-and-derive-bip380-keys/2822/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":8379,"name":"","username":"bubb1es","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/delvingbitcoin.org/bubb1es/{size}/1785_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-24T14:39:27.035Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for taking a look. There is already at \u003ccode\u003e-r\u003c/code\u003e option that only takes dice roles, so it can give “reproducable” results, ie. same dice rolls after sha256 hash always give same seed words. I compare with the results from \u003ca href=\"http://iancolman.io/bip39\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eiancolman.io/bip39\u003c/a\u003e in the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/bubb1es71/bitcoin-key-tools/blob/202a848866a666c9d855ff3157be32c1ecebd46c/seedroller/src/main.rs#L474-L509\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eknown_answer_100_rolls_no_os_entropy\u003c/a\u003e unit test.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-24T14:54:11.674Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":0.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":2822,"topic_slug":"seedroller-and-k